      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rouyn-Noranda",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1926, Rouyn and Noranda were officially constituted as cities, then merged into a single municipality in 1986.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rouyn-Noranda",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Since 1966, Rouyn‑Noranda has served as the capital of the Abitibi‑Témiscamingue region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rouyn-Noranda",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Horne Smelter, opened in 1927, remains the world’s largest processor of electronic scrap containing copper and precious metals.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
